{%- doc -%}
  Outputs what a kit's contents cost bought separately, in the shop's minor
  currency unit: the sum of the current price of every product listed in the
  kit's `custom.separate_components` metafield (one of each, first available
  variant). Outputs 0 when the metafield is empty so callers can fall back.

  This is deliberately NOT the kit's compare-at price: compare-at is shown by
  the theme as a previous price / sale, which a "bought separately" sum is not.

  Liquid can't return values from a snippet, so capture and convert:
    {% capture separate %}{% render 'nr-kit-separate-total', product: kit %}{% endcapture %}
    {% assign separate = separate | strip | plus: 0 %}

  @param {product} product - The kit product.
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign total = 0
  for component in product.metafields.custom.separate_components.value
    assign total = total | plus: component.selected_or_first_available_variant.price
  endfor
  echo total
-%}
